Water and sanitation — completion and continuing study (@wu-completion: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #source "../sources/Biological-Wastewater-Treatment-Chen-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_1AE9DK0YWQR5GDECZ9KK1JJP37", #source "../sources/Treatment-Plant-Performance-and-Water-Quality-Data.lingua#r_5PZG8VN422GHD657FBDR5KRWGS", #source "../sources/Industrial-Water-Treatment-UFC-3-230-13.lingua#r_41KNKBCA6GZWQ6VAJGAPG2HJ3R", #source "../sources/Guidelines-for-Water-Reuse-EPA-USAID.lingua#r_5D8YEK23KH0G3994XRY2JA16PK", #source "../sources/Asset-Management-for-Water-Systems-EPA.lingua#r_78ZKEFSZ16WYQ5E62DWKR8FP3N", #source "../sources/Effective-Utility-Management-EPA-USDA.lingua#r_5W9CSGM4NJKGFDES86XNMQFBRD") { r_1Y55JX0ZNS84JVY6AP315NWBFR
Completing this broad course means being able to explain and investigate a continuing water service from its source through users, treatment, collection, reuse and receiving environment. The beginning is accessible; the eventual claim requires sustained study.

Complete the introductory drinking-water course, the specified Funasa foundations, the AguaClara treatment text and public MIT treatment sequence, and the first two complete wastewater volumes. Continue through the full biological-treatment texts and [Biological Wastewater Treatment — Chen and colleagues, second edition](../sources/Biological-Wastewater-Treatment-Chen-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_1AE9DK0YWQR5GDECZ9KK1JJP37), [Assessment of Treatment Plant Performance and Water Quality Data — von Sperling, Verbyla and Oliveira](../sources/Treatment-Plant-Performance-and-Water-Quality-Data.lingua#r_5PZG8VN422GHD657FBDR5KRWGS), [Industrial Water Treatment Operation and Maintenance — UFC 3-230-13](../sources/Industrial-Water-Treatment-UFC-3-230-13.lingua#r_41KNKBCA6GZWQ6VAJGAPG2HJ3R), [Guidelines for Water Reuse — EPA and USAID, 2012](../sources/Guidelines-for-Water-Reuse-EPA-USAID.lingua#r_5D8YEK23KH0G3994XRY2JA16PK), [Asset management for small water systems — US EPA](../sources/Asset-Management-for-Water-Systems-EPA.lingua#r_78ZKEFSZ16WYQ5E62DWKR8FP3N) and [Effective utility management — rural and small systems guidebook](../sources/Effective-Utility-Management-EPA-USDA.lingua#r_5W9CSGM4NJKGFDES86XNMQFBRD) in the sequence developed here. Read the source-specific guidance needed for every defended quality or service claim. Record which edition and passages you actually studied.

Work the source, treatment, barrier/distribution, wastewater, industrial and operating section investigations. Derive and independently check the six original programs and their limits; use more detailed open models where the question requires them. Explain each major family of processes, compare meaningful alternatives and connect them through water, constituents, energy, materials, work and time.

Study all three advanced directions far enough to reconstruct their central models and criticize their evidence. Complete at least one in full research depth, along with the integrated service comparison, uncertainty study, primary-literature criticism and an independent investigation revised after substantive criticism. For a practical-completion claim, also perform and document a suitable supervised physical investigation; simulations alone establish a different kind of evidence. Completion here is an educational claim, not professional authorization or acceptance of an actual facility.

Continue into the shared chemical, fluid, thermal, electrical, geological and measurement Records as a deeper question requires them. Specialized public health, hydrology, process engineering, automation, materials and infrastructure subjects retain their own depth. Return to [Utilities](../../Utilities.lingua#r_23Z5YYXGRA1JDFD4BAM955JMNX), [Hephaestus](../../../Hephaestus.lingua#r_00000000000000000000002001) and [Ergon](../../../../Ergon.lingua#r_FE78A5A2D2A3261F711703DCC1) to follow the wider productive system. Questions about evidence and purposes connect to [Philosophy](../../../../../scholazein/philosophy/Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001).

**Return:** [Water, sanitation and industrial utilities](../Water-sanitation-and-industrial-utilities.lingua#r_7B9GRCJFHVBEEQEXKWCR2QMMPN).
